Z||000002||Raydar||09-01-2001||09:11 AM||||You don't have to replace the entire harness. There are some wires that you have to cut and splice into, though. <BR>Several Forum members have done this. Hopefully someone has the instructions in a form they can post.<BR>You can try doing a search on "gauges". It's been posted before. <P>&lt;Edited because I can't type just after waking up, either.&gt;<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||09-01-2001||09:35 AM||||Swapping out the main guage cluster is just a plug and play swap.  Adding the aux guages requires that you do a very little wiring.  <P>See here for instructions on adding the aux guages: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-01-2001||10:48 AM||||You guys can solve that "can't-type-when-I-wake-up" problem by doing what I do.  Just don't go to sleep.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
